$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(2-methoxyphenyl)-N-(2-nitrophenyl)acetamide, 6. To a solution of
2-methoxyphenyl acetic acid (6.75 g, 40.62 mmol) and 2-nitroaniline (3.76
g, 27.22 mmol) in ACN (91 mL, 0.3 M) was slowly added SOCl2 (2.96 mL,
40.62 mmol). The mixture was heated to reflux and allowed to stir for
three hours. Upon completion the reaction was concentrated to dryness.
The material was resuspended in CH2Cl2, washed with 1 M NaOH (40 mL), 1 M
HCl (40 mL), saturated NaHCO3 (40 mL), saturated NaCl (40 mL), and dried
over Na2SO4. The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography,
2-(2-methoxyphenyl)-N-(2-nitrophenyl)acetamide (7.17 g, 92.0% yield).
1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.36 (s, 1H), 8.76 (dd, J=8.8, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
8.14 (dd, J=8.8, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.62-7.58 (m, 1H), 7.37-7.31 (m, 2H),
7.15-7.11 (m, 1H), 7.02-6.93 (m, 2H), 3.91 (s, 3H), 3.82 (s, 2H). 13C-NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.6, 157.1, 136.4, 135.6, 134.8, 131.3, 129.4,
125.5, 122.9, 122.3, 122.0, 121.0, 110.7, 55.3, 40.5.
