$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
6-(2-Amino-pyrimidin-4-yloxy)-naphthalene-1-carboxylic Acid
(4-Fluoro-3-trifluoromethyl-phenyl)-amide (4). Compound 3 (2.1 g; 7.8
mmol) was suspended in DMF (50 mL). Et3N (11 mL; 79 mmol), DMAP (0.42 g;
3.4 mmol), 4-fluoro-3-trifluoromethyl-aniline (1.6 mL; 9.7 mmol), and T3P
(9.1 mL; 15.6 mmol) were added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h
at rt, concentrated in vacuo, and the residue redissolved in EtOAc and
water. The aq layer was separated off and reextracted with EtOAc (2×).
Washing the org layers with water and brine, drying (Na2SO4),
evaporation, and column chromatography (SiO2; CH2Cl2/EtOAc 4:1 → 1:2).
6-(6-Chloro-pyrimidin-4-yloxy)-naphthalene-1-carboxylic Acid
(3-Trifluoromethyl-phenyl)-amide (12). Compound 12 was prepared
analogously to 4 (13.6 g; 92%). MS: [M + 1]+ = 444. 1H NMR (CDCl3-d) δ
[ppm]: 8.61 (1H, s), 8.52 (1H, d, J = 9 Hz), 8.04 (1H, s), 8.01 (1H, d, J
= 9 Hz), 7.93 (2H, m), 7.80 (1H, d, J = 7 Hz), 7.72 (1H, d, J = 2), 7.58
(2H, m), 7.49 (1H, d, J = 8), 7.42(1H, dd, J = 9 Hz/ 3 Hz), 7.05 (1H, s).
