$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure II ( for cat.2, cat4,
cat.7-9) N-Cbz-amino acid (10 mmol) was dissolved in THF (25 mL) and
cooled in an ice bath. NMM (10 mmol) and ethyl chloroformate ( 10 mmol)
were added to the aboved cooled solution and stirred for 30min. The
resulting mixture was treated with sulfonyl hydrazide (1.2 eq, 12mmol) or
hydroxylamine derivatives at 0 °C. After 2h the solvent THF was
evaporated and the residue was dissolved in DCM (200 mL). Then the DCM
layer was washed with hydrogen chloride solution (2M, 60×3 mL) and brine
subsequently. The solvent was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and evaporated
in vacuum. The crude product which could be used in next step directly.
The deprotection of the above crude product was performed in the presence
of Pd/C (1mmol, 10 mol%) in methanol (50 mmol) under the atmosphere of
hydrogen. The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature
overnight. When the reaction completed, the reaction mixture was filtered
and the solvent was removed in vacuum. The obtained mixture was further
purified by flash chromatography ( DCM/Methanol = 20/1 ).
(S)-2-amino-N-methoxy-3-phenylpropanamide (cat.7): white solid in 91 %
yield. M.p. 137-141 °C. [α]D 20 +6.0 (c = 1.1, DMF); 1H NMR (400MHz,
d6-DMSO): δ 7.28-7.17 (m, 5H), 3.47 (s, 3H), 3.24-3.21 (t, J = 6.8 Hz,
1H), 2.85-2.80 (dd, J = 13.2 Hz, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.69-2.64 (dd, J = 7.4
Hz, J = 13.2 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, d6-DMSO): δ 170.80, 138.38,
129.28, 128.025, 126.08, 62.88, 54.40, 41.27; IR (film, ν/cm-1 ): 3350,
3168, 2977, 2935, 1793, 1684, 1494, 1448, 1057, 1024, 920, 746, 700; HRMS
(ESI) m/z calcd for C10H14N2O2 [M+Na]+ 217.0953, found 217.0953.
