$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2S,3S)-Benzyl
2-((S)-2-((((9H-fluoren-9-yl)methoxy)carbonyl)(methyl)amino)-3-methylbutanamido)-3-((tert-butyldiphenylsilyl)
oxy)butanoate (S7) To a stirred solution of
N-α-(9-Fluorenylmethyoxycarbonyl)-L-valine (192 mg, 0.52 mmol), HBTU (250
mg, 0.66 mmol), HOBt (96.8 mg, 0.72 mmol) and DMF (2 mL) was added a DMF
solution (3 mL) of S6 (195.3 mg, 0.44 mmol) at room temperature. Then,
DIEA (152 μL, 0.87 mmol) was added to the mixture, which was stirred for
3.5 h. The reaction was quenched by adding saturated aqueous NH4Cl (15
mL) and water (10 mL), and then the resulting mixture was extracted with
EtOAc (2 x 30 ml). Combined extracts were washed by brine (2 x 50 mL),
dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under a reduced pressure. The crude
material was subjected to silica gel flash chromatography (hexane/EtOAc
4:1). S7 (310.8 mg, 91%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.76
(m, 2H), 7.63-7.61 (m, 2H), 7.59-7.57 (m, 3H), 7.53 (m, 1H), 7.42-7.26
(m, 15H), 6.67 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.18 (d, J = 12.3 Hz, 1H), 5.10 (d, J
= 12.3 Hz, 1H), 4.63 (dd, J = 3.4, 7.4 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (dd, J = 10.0, 13.4
Hz, 1H), 4.25-4.22 (m, 2H), 4.15 (d, J = 10.9 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (m, 1H), 2.91
(s, 3H), 2.28 (m, 1H), 1.02 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 0.98 (s, 9H), 0.93 (d, J
= 6.3 Hz, 3H), 0.86 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) 170.2,
169.5, 157.3, 144.1, 141.5, 135.9, 135.4, 133.8, 132.9, 130.1, 129.8,
128.7, 128.4, 127.9, 127.9, 127.7, 127.2, 125.2, 125., 120.2, 70.3, 67.9,
67.2, 65.4, 58.4, 47.4, 30.1, 26.9, 26.5, 19.8, 19.6, 19.3, 18.8; IR
(neat) 2962, 1743, 1688; [α]D 26 -37.3 (c 1.98, CHCl3), HR-FAB-MS m/z
783.3813 [M+H]+ (calcd. for C48H55N2O6Si 783.3829, Δ = 1.6 mmu).
